# Own-wording Tome of Heroes magic items, chunk A (Alseid's Peony to Floodmote Heartglow Lantern). Row shape as tkdm_item_a.py.
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

def add(name, typ, rar, att, text, **o):
    ITEMS.append((name, typ, rar, att, text, o))

_W = "Worts are the magical herbs of Tome of Heroes. Each plant has a Minor Wort anyone can use, a Ceremony Wort that needs a ritual and a number of cuttings, and a Cultivated Wort that appears in a garden grown for the stated time. "
_HG = "A heartglow lantern is a hexagonal crystal in a metal frame that burns no fuel, so it suits caverns where air is scarce. While holding it, use an action to make it shed bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for 20 feet more. The light lasts until you use a bonus action to repeat the command word, or until no living creature holds or carries it. Each lantern gains an extra effect when infused with vitality. A creature touching it can use an action to infuse it, lowering that creature's hit point maximum by its Proficiency Bonus until it finishes a rest, and the lantern gains charges equal to that amount. A lantern can hold any number of charges from any number of creatures, but each creature can infuse a given lantern only once between long rests. "

add("Alseid's Peony", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: guidance, secrets, teamwork. Found in druidic circles, along animal paths, beside anthills. A flowering plant with large, many-petaled blooms in white, pink and red, with bright yellow centers, closing at night or in cloud. **Minor Wort.** As an action, tear off a bloom to summon a small red-petaled bloomling. It uses the awakened shrub statistics, lasts 1 hour or until destroyed, and is friendly to you and your companions. It rolls its own Initiative, obeys your verbal commands with no action from you, and if given none, defends itself and does nothing else. When it ends or is destroyed it crumbles to petals and sticks. **Ceremony Wort (3rd level).** Holding a handful of petals, spend 10 minutes concentrating on a place, then scatter the petals. They land as an arrow pointing toward it. They scatter without forming an arrow if the place does not exist or lies on another plane. A clump forms at the arrow's point if a major obstacle lies between, such as a magical barrier, a miles-long wall, a desert or a river. Needs 2 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort.** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks whispers secrets, lore and rumors. Each bloom repeats, in the original voice and language, any words spoken in the garden since it first bloomed. To those nearby it sounds like wind in leaves, but a creature can put an ear to a bloom to hear everything. The peonies have no intelligence and do not tell truth from lies or past from present, and in very old gardens may whisper fragments out of order or from different years. Zone of truth cannot be cast within 100 feet of the garden, though creatures that naturally tell truth from lies, like planetars, know which whispers are false.")
add("Argent Mantle", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "A finely made hood-and-shoulder piece reserved for ranking knights of devout or monastic military orders, granting exceptional skill in battle, statecraft and leadership. Use a bonus action to speak a command word, and a golden nimbus surrounds your head, shedding bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for 20 feet more. Friendly creatures in that bright light have Advantage on Initiative rolls and cannot be Surprised unless incapacitated. The nimbus lasts until you repeat the command word as a bonus action or take the mantle off. **Endearing Leader.** While wearing it, use an action to raise your Charisma score to 20 for 10 minutes. It does nothing if your Charisma is already 20 or higher. Once used, you cannot use it again until the next dawn.", ch=[1, "1", "dawn"])
add("Asphodel", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: death, sacrifice, passage to and from the afterlife. Found on battlefields, in graveyards and on hilltops. A hardy flowering plant with tufted leaves on long stems and white or yellow flowers. **Minor Wort.** As an action, eat half a bloom and put the rest in a dead creature's mouth to see the last minute of its life through its eyes. Afterward make a DC 15 Constitution save or gain one level of Exhaustion. **Ceremony Wort (4th level).** Bury a prized possession of at least uncommon rarity beside the plant (1 minute of work) to have Advantage on death saving throws for 4 hours. Up to five others can join, each burying their own possession. A creature can dig its item up at any time, ending the effect for its owner. A creature that benefited cannot do so again for 3 days. It needs a whole, healthy asphodel plant to bury beside, and no set number of cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (9th level).** A garden grown for at least 12 weeks can raise a creature dead no more than 1 year and 1 day that did not die of old age. After 1d8 hours in the field, it returns to life as if by the resurrection spell. The field then withers and cannot be regrown for 10 years and 1 day. The gardener can set limits on the effect, such as humanoids only or a required password.")
add("Beads of Contemplation", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 1, "A strand of eight wooden beads carved with geometric patterns on a stout cord. The beads store ki energy for later use, up to 8 ki points. At the end of a rest, touch them and spend ki points equal to half your Proficiency Bonus to place ki in them. While wearing or carrying them, use a bonus action to take any number of ki points out, regaining that many and freeing space in the beads. Requires attunement by a monk.", by="Monk")
add("Bloodspeed Elixir", "Potion", "Rare", 0, "A murky crimson liquid, thick as sludge, smelling of ozone. When you drink it, your speed triples for 1 minute. If you take the Dash action while it lasts, you take 2d6 Poison damage as your body is pushed past its limits.")
add("Bright Bishop Sage", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _W + "Themes: protection, sanctuary, purification. Found at churches and temples, outside kitchen doors, and near druidic circles. An evergreen shrub with woody stems, small blue and purple flowers, and short, broad, softly furred leaves. **Minor Wort.** As an action, burn a bundle to protect one creature, doorway or object. The creature is protected as by protection from evil and good, but only against celestials, fiends and undead. **Ceremony Wort.** As an action, sprinkle chopped sage on or in up to six plates, bowls or glasses of nonmagical food or drink, purifying them of poison and disease. Needs 2 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (9th level).** A garden grown for at least 8 weeks is guarded by heavenly magic. Aberrations, elementals, fey, fiends and undead cannot enter the garden or come within 15 feet of it, and bodies interred within it or 15 feet around cannot become undead.")
add("Campaign Field Tent", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "Use an action to set this 1-inch cloth cube on the ground and speak its command word. It grows into a field tent, with sides open or closed as you choose, that lasts until you speak the command word as an action to dismiss it, which works only if the tent is empty. The canvas tent is 15 feet on a side and 10 feet high. It stays firmly fixed to the ground, even on bare stone, a ship's deck or loose sand, and its magic keeps it from tipping. Each creature in the area where it appears makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 5d10 Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success, and is pushed to a free space outside but next to the tent. Unworn, uncarried objects there take the damage and are pushed automatically. The tent has 50 hit points, immunity to nonmagical attacks (siege weapons excluded) and Resistance to all other damage. Inside are a small table, a chair and five simple folding beds. It holds up to six Medium or smaller creatures. A creature finishing a rest in it regains double the hit points from Hit Dice it spends, reduces its Exhaustion by 2 instead of 1, and has Advantage on saves against disease and poison while resting there.")
add("Cestus +1", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, "Leather hand wraps padded across the knuckles. While wearing them you have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with unarmed strikes. The bonus follows the item's rarity.", fx={"atk": 1, "dmg": 1})
add("Cestus +2", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, "Leather hand wraps padded across the knuckles. While wearing them you have a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls with unarmed strikes. The bonus follows the item's rarity.", fx={"atk": 2, "dmg": 2})
add("Cestus +3", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, "Leather hand wraps padded across the knuckles. While wearing them you have a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls with unarmed strikes. The bonus follows the item's rarity.", fx={"atk": 3, "dmg": 3})
add("Chain Cilice", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, "A bracelet of spiked chain made to fit an ankle, wrist or thigh. While wearing it, use an action to speak its command word. It tightens on your skin, dealing 1d6 Piercing damage to you at the start of each of your turns until you use a bonus action to end it. If you have the Ki feature, or ki points from another source such as the Inner Resilience feat, you regain 1 ki point for every 5 damage it causes. If it would reduce you to 0 hit points, it reduces you to 1 instead and its effect ends. If it ended this way, you cannot use it again until the next dawn.")
add("Champion's Lavender", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _W + "Themes: devotion, swift healing, truth. Found near shrines, where vows were honored, and after steadfast vigils. A flowering shrub with narrow leaves and blue, violet or lilac flowers on spike-like stems. **Minor Wort.** As an action, press a sprig to a creature's wound to close it quickly and ease pain or fatigue. The target can immediately spend one Hit Die to regain hit points as at the end of a rest, or make a DC 13 Constitution save to recover from one level of Exhaustion on a success. **Ceremony Wort (3rd level).** Spend 10 minutes chanting and walking the edge of an area no larger than a 40-foot cube while waving a bundle of lit, smoking lavender, to make a ward against unseen intruders. With a censer to concentrate the smoke, the ward can cover an 80-foot cube. It lasts 8 hours. An invisible creature inside it glows purple, and each creature that was present when you warded the area senses its presence. **Cultivated Wort (5th level).** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks is a shrine to truth. A trespassing creature that has broken a vow, or intentionally deceived someone and caused great harm, is marked with a dim purple mark, symbol or rune chosen by the gardener, usually one meaning guilt, until it leaves. The mark does not appear if the creature has found justice or redemption for the act, such as paying fines, serving the community or atoning at a temple. The garden does not tell broken vows from deceptions, and does not mark minor or unknowing deceptions such as unkept plans or spreading misinformation without knowing.")
add("Chaunic Clover", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: prosperity, luck, risk. Found at the end of rainbows, near fairy circles, and where major breakthroughs or successes happened. A low, sprawling plant with leaves in threes or fours and small, spiky flowers in white, purple or yellow. **Minor Wort.** As an action, put a sprig in a pouch of copper or silver pieces totaling no more than 99 and roll a d100. If the roll is higher than the number of coins, the coins double. On a 100, they double and each coin becomes gold. On a 1, all the coins are destroyed and a fey creature on your plane learns of your failure and takes an interest in you. The sprig is destroyed either way. **Ceremony Wort.** As an action, place a pot, kettle or cup holding a sprig under the shade of an old tree to summon a magic cauldron for 10 minutes. The first time, it is empty and becomes bound to you, and each later use summons the same one. When not summoned, it sits in a tiny demiplane that only a wish spell can reach. It holds only coins, but any number. You can dismiss it early as an action. If you die, it is no longer bound to you, becomes nonmagical, and appears in the shade beneath one of the trees where you summoned it, holding your coins. If you return to life and use the wort again, you bind a new empty cauldron. Needs 1 cutting. **Cultivated Wort (8th level).** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks makes nearby plant life healthy and abundant. Within 1 mile, plants grow lush and resist disease, crops double their yield, and plant creatures are 60 percent more likely to be neutral or friendly instead of hostile.")
add("Cloak of Tentacles", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1, "The cloak settles on your shoulders like a writhing creature, warm to the touch yet icy against the skin. **Shimmering Skin.** Use an action to show its shimmering lining. Each creature within 10 feet that sees you makes a DC 15 Wisdom save or is Incapacitated until the end of its next turn. Once used, you cannot use this again until the next dawn. **Writhing Tentacles.** Use a bonus action to make the cloak sprout four tentacles for 1 minute. When a creature within 10 feet hits you with a melee attack, a tentacle lashes at the attacker with a +7 bonus to hit. On a hit it deals 2d10 Bludgeoning damage, then goes still and inert. When the duration ends or all four are inert, you cannot use this again until the next dawn.")
add("Deadbane Heartglow Lantern", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _HG + "**Deadbane.** While holding it, use an action and spend 1 or more charges to make it detect undead for 1 hour. When an undead is within 20 feet, the light turns blue and grows brighter the closer the undead is. Each charge beyond the first adds 30 minutes and 5 feet to the detection distance. The extra distance does not enlarge the light.")
add("Deepstone Cestus", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 1, "Leather hand wraps fitted with round, flat stones engraved with runes. While wearing them, your ki save DC increases by 2. Requires attunement by a monk.", by="Monk")
add("Emperor's Garlic", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: authority, immunity, sight beyond sight. Found among wildflowers, near ancient trees, and in ruins or lairs once held by very wise creatures. A flowering plant growing from a bulb, with flat blade-like leaves and a sphere of pink and purple flowers atop a tall stem. **Minor Wort.** Eat a raw clove as an action to gain Resistance to Poison damage and Advantage on saves against Poisoned for 1 hour, but Disadvantage on all Deception and Persuasion checks for that time. If you already resist Poison, you become immune instead. **Ceremony Wort (3rd level).** Use a bulb as a spell focus so that you and at least two other characters can perform an exorcism on a possessed target for 1 minute. Each must keep Concentration and stay within 30 feet of the target. It fails if no one is concentrating or all are more than 30 feet away, and then you cannot try again for 24 hours. At the end, if at least one character kept Concentration, the target is freed as if by the break enchantment effect of dispel evil and good. The garlic is consumed whether it works or not. Needs 4 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (5th level).** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks guards the area against undead. An undead that starts its turn in or within 100 feet of the garden makes a Charisma save or is turned.")
add("Esquire's Rowels", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1, "Silver-chased spurs. While riding a mount and wearing them, you have a +1 bonus to Initiative rolls and your mount's AC rises by 2. You and your mount also have Advantage on Constitution saves against Exhaustion from traveling more than 8 hours in a day.")
add("Far Traveler's Freesia", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", 0, _W + "Themes: friendship, trust, purity, innocence. Found at shorelines, alongside crossroads, and outside inns, taverns and trading posts. A flowering plant with long, narrow leaves and conical flowers in white, red and yellow. **Minor Wort.** As an action, give a gift of freesia to one creature to win it over. A hostile target makes a Wisdom save or becomes indifferent toward you, with Disadvantage for a beast with Intelligence 3 or lower. **Ceremony Wort.** Soak freesia in a bowl of holy water for 10 minutes, then brush the water on the brows of a number of creatures equal to 1 + your Proficiency Bonus. Each has Advantage on ability checks and saves against Exhaustion and gains 1d6 temporary hit points for 8 hours. Needs 2 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort.** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks attracts friendly moths and butterflies. One that feeds on the freesia for at least 24 hours gains Intelligence 6 and can speak Common and one other language of the gardener. The insects are always at least indifferent to other creatures in the garden and usually help with simple tasks that keep them within the garden for no more than 24 hours.")
add("Fiery Snapdragon", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 0, _W + "Themes: fire, strength, presence. Found in areas burned by forest fires, beside scorch marks from fire magic, and near sun temples. A flowering plant with tall, narrow stalks, leaves spiraling around each, and flowers shaped like a dragon's open maw in yellow, pink and red. **Minor Wort.** As an action, put a sprig in the flame of a lit torch so that any creature carrying it has Resistance to Fire damage. The torch's remaining duration shortens to 10 minutes, unless already shorter. A creature carrying it can use a bonus action to snuff it and gain immunity to Fire damage until the start of its next turn. The torch then crumbles to dust. **Ceremony Wort (5th level).** Build a bonfire laden with snapdragon and perform a ritual of strength on one creature within 10 feet. You and the target stay in the heat for 10 minutes, and at the end the target's Strength score becomes 25 for 1 hour. Needs 4 cuttings. **Cultivated Wort (9th level).** A garden grown for at least 4 weeks repels dragons. A dragon that starts its turn in or within 150 feet of it makes a Wisdom save or is turned, as by Turn Undead. Draconic creatures like chimeras or kobolds can be turned too, but have Advantage on the save.")
add("Fletcher's Retort Gloves", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", 1, "While wearing these gloves and using Deflect Missiles, you can spend 1 ki point to reduce the damage by 1d10 + your Dexterity modifier + twice your monk level instead. If that reduces it to 0 and you spend 1 ki point to throw the missile, the attack has a normal range of 30 feet and a long range of 120 feet. When a friendly creature within 5 feet of you is hit by a ranged weapon attack while you wear them, you can use Deflect Missiles to deflect or catch the missile. Requires attunement by a monk.", by="Monk")
add("Floodmote Heartglow Lantern", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", 0, _HG + "**Floodmote.** If you are submerged while holding it, use a Reaction and spend 1 or more charges to create a bubble of air around you for 1 hour. Each charge beyond the first adds 1 hour and lets you protect one more creature within 30 feet. The bubble surrounds only the head or other air-breathing organ and supplies breathable air for the duration.")
